    "role": "user",
    "content": "Program: CBACT04C. Input files and their record layouts:\n\nTCATBAL: CVTRA01Y TRAN-CAT-BAL-RECORD (50 bytes)\n  TRANCAT-ACCT-ID              9(11)\n  TRANCAT-TYPE-CD              X(2)\n  TRANCAT-CD                   9(4)\n  TRAN-CAT-BAL                 S9(9)V9(2)\n\nXREF: CVACT03Y CARD-XREF-RECORD (50 bytes)\n  XREF-CARD-NUM                X(16)\n  XREF-CUST-ID                 9(9)\n  XREF-ACCT-ID                 9(11)\n\nACCOUNT: CVACT01Y ACCOUNT-RECORD (300 bytes)\n  ACCT-ID                      9(11)\n  ACCT-ACTIVE-STATUS           X(1)\n  ACCT-CURR-BAL                S9(10)V9(2)\n  ACCT-CREDIT-LIMIT            S9(10)V9(2)\n  ACCT-CASH-CREDIT-LIMIT       S9(10)V9(2)\n  ACCT-OPEN-DATE               X(10)\n  ACCT-EXPIRAION-DATE          X(10)\n  ACCT-REISSUE-DATE            X(10)\n  ACCT-CURR-CYC-CREDIT         S9(10)V9(2)\n  ACCT-CURR-CYC-DEBIT          S9(10)V9(2)\n  ACCT-ADDR-ZIP                X(10)\n  ACCT-GROUP-ID                X(10)\n\nDISCGRP: CVTRA02Y DIS-GROUP-RECORD (50 bytes)\n  DIS-ACCT-GROUP-ID            X(10)\n  DIS-TRAN-TYPE-CD             X(2)\n  DIS-TRAN-CAT-CD              9(4)\n  DIS-INT-RATE                 S9(4)V9(2)\nThe program runs with job PARM '2022071800'. Account, cross-reference and disclosure group files are read by key, so every category balance's account needs ACCOUNT and XREF records.\n\nRule to test:\n{\n \"id\": \"BR-CBACT04C-001\",\n \"title\": \"Account balance update when the account number changes\",\n \"summary\": \"Category balance records are processed in key order and grouped by consecutive account ID. When a record's account ID differs from the previous one, and this is not the first record, the previous account is updated before the new account is loaded. The update adds the group's total interest to the current balance, sets the cycle credit and debit to zero and rewrites the account record.\",\n \"given\": [\n  {\n   \"text\": \"At program start, the first-record flag WS-FIRST-TIME is 'Y'.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"WS-FIRST-TIME\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": [\n    \"Y\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"text\": \"At program start, the last-seen account number WS-LAST-ACCT-NUM is spaces, so the first record always looks like a new account.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"WS-LAST-ACCT-NUM\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": []\n  },\n  {\n   \"text\": \"TCATBAL-FILE is an indexed file read with sequential access, so category balance records arrive in order of the record key FD-TRAN-CAT-KEY.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"TCATBAL-FILE\",\n    \"FD-TRAN-CAT-KEY\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": []\n  },\n  {\n   \"text\": \"Each category balance record is read, one at a time, into TRAN-CAT-BAL-RECORD.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"TCATBAL-FILE\",\n    \"TRAN-CAT-BAL-RECORD\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": []\n  },\n  {\n   \"text\": \"Interest is computed for a category balance record, and added to the group total, only when the looked-up rate DIS-INT-RATE is not zero.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"DIS-INT-RATE\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": []\n  },\n  {\n   \"text\": \"Each computed monthly interest amount is added to the running account total WS-TOTAL-INT.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"WS-MONTHLY-INT\",\n    \"WS-TOTAL-INT\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": []\n  }\n ],\n \"when\": [\n  {\n   \"text\": \"A category balance record is read whose TRANCAT-ACCT-ID differs from WS-LAST-ACCT-NUM, and WS-FIRST-TIME is not 'Y'.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"TRANCAT-ACCT-ID\",\n    \"WS-LAST-ACCT-NUM\",\n    \"WS-FIRST-TIME\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": [\n    \"Y\"\n   ]\n  }\n ],\n \"then\": [\n  {\n   \"text\": \"The account update runs before the new account is read. As a result, ACCOUNT-RECORD still holds the previous account when it is updated.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"FD-ACCT-ID\",\n    \"TRANCAT-ACCT-ID\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": []\n  },\n  {\n   \"text\": \"The previous account's current balance ACCT-CURR-BAL is increased by WS-TOTAL-INT (an add with no rounding). This happens even when the total is zero because every category had a zero rate.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"WS-TOTAL-INT\",\n    \"ACCT-CURR-BAL\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": []\n  },\n  {\n   \"text\": \"ACCT-CURR-BAL holds 10 integer digits and 2 decimals, signed.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"ACCT-CURR-BAL\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": []\n  },\n  {\n   \"text\": \"WS-TOTAL-INT holds 9 integer digits and 2 decimals, signed.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"WS-TOTAL-INT\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": []\n  },\n  {\n   \"text\": \"The previous account's current-cycle credit ACCT-CURR-CYC-CREDIT and current-cycle debit ACCT-CURR-CYC-DEBIT are both set to zero.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"ACCT-CURR-CYC-CREDIT\",\n    \"ACCT-CURR-CYC-DEBIT\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": []\n  },\n  {\n   \"text\": \"The account record is rewritten in place from ACCOUNT-RECORD. All other account fields keep the values that were read.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"FD-ACCTFILE-REC\",\n    \"ACCOUNT-RECORD\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": []\n  },\n  {\n   \"text\": \"On the very first record, no update is done. Instead, WS-FIRST-TIME is set to 'N'.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"WS-FIRST-TIME\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": [\n    \"N\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"text\": \"In both cases, WS-TOTAL-INT is reset to 0 and WS-LAST-ACCT-NUM is set to the new TRANCAT-ACCT-ID.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"WS-TOTAL-INT\",\n    \"WS-LAST-ACCT-NUM\",\n    \"TRANCAT-ACCT-ID\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": []\n  },\n  {\n   \"text\": \"TRANCAT-ACCT-ID is copied to both FD-ACCT-ID and FD-XREF-ACCT-ID, and the new account and its card cross-reference are then read.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"TRANCAT-ACCT-ID\",\n    \"FD-ACCT-ID\",\n    \"FD-XREF-ACCT-ID\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": []\n  },\n  {\n   \"text\": \"The card cross-reference is read into CARD-XREF-RECORD using FD-XREF-ACCT-ID as the key.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"CARD-XREF-RECORD\",\n    \"FD-XREF-ACCT-ID\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": []\n  },\n  {\n   \"text\": \"FD-XREF-ACCT-ID is declared as an alternate record key of XREF-FILE.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"FD-XREF-ACCT-ID\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": []\n  }\n ]\n}"
   }
